lestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2023-02-01T16:08:35Z","updated_at":"2023-02-01T16:20:18Z","closed_at":"2023-02-01T16:19:27Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"It is not a typing issue, I just want to report an error in the documentation of Basic Relationship Patterns in the Late-Evaluation of Relationship Arguments section, to be specific, line 1050 of the file: [basic_relationships.rst](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/main/doc/build/orm/basic_relationships.rst)\r\n\r\nThe parentheses of the function should not go, because if we leave the parentheses, the function will be executed when the application is initialized and it may be possible to throw an ImportError exception\r\n\r\n### Suggested Change\r\n\r\nJust remove the parentheses from the Late-Evaluaton function\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport typing\r\n\r\n    from sqlalchemy import desc\r\n\r\n    if typing.TYPE_CHECKING:\r\n        from myapplication import Child\r\n\r\n\r\n    def _resolve_child_model():\r\n        from myapplication import Child\r\n\r\n        return Child\r\n\r\n\r\n    class Parent(Base):\r\n        # ...\r\n\r\n        children: Mapped[List[\"Child\"]] = relationship(\r\n            # _resolve_child_model() Raise ImportError\r\n            # _resolve_child_model or lambda: _resolve_child_model() Correct\r\n            _resolve_child_model,\r\n            order_by=lambda: desc(_resolve_child_model().email_address),\r\n            primaryjoin=lambda: Parent.id == _resolve_child_model().parent_id,\r\n        )\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Versions\r\n\r\n- OS: Manjaro Linux\r\n- Python: 3.10\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 2.0\r\n- Type checker (eg: mypy 0.991, pyright 1.1.290, etc): pyright with Pylance","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avat